### Kirana backend — Phase 1 manual tests
### VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client),
### then click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom.
### Re-running? Change the phone numbers below or you'll get 409 PHONE_TAKEN.

@base = http://localhost:8080/api
@customerPhone = 9876500001
@ownerPhone = 9876500002

### 1. Health (public) -> 200 {"status":"OK"}
GET {{base}}/health

### 2. Register a customer (Hindi name) -> 201 {token, user}
# @name registerCustomer
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "सीता देवी",
  "phone": "{{customerPhone}}",
  "password": "secret1",
  "role": "CUSTOMER"
}

### 3. Same phone again -> 409 PHONE_TAKEN
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Someone Else",
  "phone": "{{customerPhone}}",
  "password": "secret2",
  "role": "CUSTOMER"
}

### 4. Invalid input -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with fields.name / phone / password
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "phone": "12345",
  "password": "abc",
  "role": "CUSTOMER"
}

### 5. Bad role -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR, fields.role = "must be one of [CUSTOMER, STORE_OWNER]"
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "phone": "9876500099",
  "password": "secret1",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### 6. Login (customer) -> 200 {token, user}
# @name loginCustomer
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{customerPhone}}",
  "password": "secret1"
}

@customerToken = {{loginCustomer.response.body.token}}

### 7. Wrong password -> 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{customerPhone}}",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 8. Unknown phone -> 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS (same message as 7)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000000",
  "password": "secret1"
}

### 9. /me without token -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{base}}/me

### 10. /me with a garbage token -> 401 "Invalid token"
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.token

### 11. /me with token -> 200 user
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 12. Switch language to Hindi -> 200, preferredLang "hi"
PATCH {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "preferredLang": "hi"
}

### 13. Change name -> 200, new name
PATCH {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "सीता शर्मा"
}

### 14. Bad language -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR, fields.preferredLang
PATCH {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "preferredLang": "fr"
}

### 15. Customer hitting a store-owner path -> 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{base}}/store/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 16. Register a store owner -> 201
# @name registerOwner
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Gupta Kirana",
  "phone": "{{ownerPhone}}",
  "password": "secret1",
  "role": "STORE_OWNER"
}

@ownerToken = {{registerOwner.response.body.token}}

### 17. Store owner hitting a customer path -> 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{base}}/requests/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 18. Store owner on own store path -> 404 NOT_FOUND (allowed, no endpoint until Phase 3)
GET {{base}}/store/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


######################################################################
### PHASE 2 — STORES
### Uses the dev seed data (printed in the app console on first run).
### Seed customers: 9000000001-03, store owners: 9000000011-25, password test123.
### Test location: Noida 28.5050, 77.3800
######################################################################

@lat = 28.5050
@lng = 77.3800

### 2.1 Log in as seed customer (Anita Singh)
# @name seedCustomer
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000001",
  "password": "test123"
}

@cToken = {{seedCustomer.response.body.token}}

### 2.2 Log in as seed store owner (Sharma General Store)
# @name seedOwner
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000011",
  "password": "test123"
}

@oToken = {{seedOwner.response.body.token}}

### 2.3 Owner: my store -> 200, includes phone
GET {{base}}/stores/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{oToken}}

### 2.4 Owner: second store -> 409 STORE_EXISTS
POST {{base}}/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{oToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another Store",
  "address": "Shop 99, Main Market",
  "area": "Sector 93",
  "lat": 28.5050,
  "lng": 77.3800
}

### 2.5 Owner: close the store -> 200, isOpen false
PATCH {{base}}/stores/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{oToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isOpen": false
}

### 2.6 Customer: nearby -> 7 stores now (Sharma is closed); no phone field
GET {{base}}/stores/nearby?lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.7 Owner: reopen the store -> 200, isOpen true
PATCH {{base}}/stores/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{oToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isOpen": true
}

### 2.8 Customer: nearby -> 8 stores, 0.2 km ... 2.9 km, Sharma first
GET {{base}}/stores/nearby?lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.9 Customer: search by area -> 3 stores in Sector 128 (incl. Om Sai at 3.8 km)
GET {{base}}/stores/search?q=sector%20128&lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.10 Customer: search by name -> all "kirana" stores, closed ones have isOpen false
GET {{base}}/stores/search?q=KIRANA&lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.11 Customer: Hindi search -> हरि ओम किराना at 5.0 km
GET {{base}}/stores/search?q=किराना&lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.12 Customer: search without location -> sorted by name, distanceKm null
GET {{base}}/stores/search?q=store
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.13 Customer: empty q -> same as nearby
GET {{base}}/stores/search?q=&lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.14a Helper: capture Sharma General Store's id (run before 2.14b)
# @name ownerStore
GET {{base}}/stores/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{oToken}}

@seedOwnerStoreId = {{ownerStore.response.body.id}}

### 2.14b Customer: store page -> 200, distanceKm 0.2, no phone
GET {{base}}/stores/{{seedOwnerStoreId}}?lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.15 Customer: unknown store -> 404 STORE_NOT_FOUND
GET {{base}}/stores/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.16 Customer calling owner endpoint -> 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{base}}/stores/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.17 Owner calling customer endpoint -> 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{base}}/stores/nearby?lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{oToken}}

### 2.18 Bad coordinates -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR, fields.lat
GET {{base}}/stores/nearby?lat=200&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}

### 2.19 New owner with no store: register, then GET mine -> 404 NO_STORE
# @name newOwner
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "New Owner",
  "phone": "9876500003",
  "password": "secret1",
  "role": "STORE_OWNER"
}

@nToken = {{newOwner.response.body.token}}

### 2.20 New owner: GET mine -> 404 NO_STORE
GET {{base}}/stores/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{nToken}}

### 2.21 New owner: invalid store -> 400 with fields.name, address, lat
POST {{base}}/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{nToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "address": "",
  "area": "Sector 135",
  "lat": 95,
  "lng": 77.38
}

### 2.22 New owner: create store (Hindi name, no phone -> owner's phone) -> 201
POST {{base}}/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{nToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "श्री राम किराना",
  "address": "Shop 7, Market Road",
  "area": "Sector 135",
  "lat": 28.5100,
  "lng": 77.3850
}

### 2.23 Customer: Hindi search finds the new store too (0.7 km away)
GET {{base}}/stores/search?q=राम&lat={{lat}}&lng={{lng}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cToken}}


######################################################################
### PHASE 3 — TYPED REQUESTS
### Run 2.1 / 2.2 first if you haven't (they set @lat, @lng and tokens),
### or just run the two logins below.
### Seed requests #1-#4 already exist; Sharma General Store (9000000011)
### and Gupta Kirana (9000000012) received all four.
######################################################################

### 3.1 Login as seed customer Anita (9000000001)
# @name p3Customer
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000001",
  "password": "test123"
}

@p3c = {{p3Customer.response.body.token}}

### 3.2 Create a NEAREST request -> 201, 5 targets sorted by distance, status OPEN
# @name nearestReq
POST {{base}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "NEAREST",
  "lat": 28.5050,
  "lng": 77.3800,
  "items": [
    { "name": "Aashirvaad atta", "quantity": 5, "unit": "KG" },
    { "name": "चीनी", "quantity": 2, "unit": "KG" },
    { "name": "Amul butter", "quantity": 1, "unit": "PACKET" },
    { "name": "अंडे", "quantity": 1, "unit": "DOZEN" },
    { "name": "Haldi", "quantity": 250, "unit": "G" },
    { "name": "Doodh", "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "L" }
  ]
}

@nearestId = {{nearestReq.response.body.id}}

### 3.3 Find a store for DIRECT (Gupta Kirana; copy nothing, id is captured)
# @name gupta
GET {{base}}/stores/search?q=gupta&lat=28.5050&lng=77.3800
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}

@guptaId = {{gupta.response.body.$[0].id}}

### 3.4 Create a DIRECT request to Gupta Kirana -> 201, exactly 1 target
# @name directReq
POST {{base}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "DIRECT",
  "storeId": {{guptaId}},
  "lat": 28.5050,
  "lng": 77.3800,
  "items": [
    { "name": "Tata salt", "quantity": 1, "unit": "KG" },
    { "name": "Parle-G", "quantity": 2, "unit": "PACKET" }
  ]
}

@directId = {{directReq.response.body.id}}

### 3.5 DIRECT to a closed store (Agarwal Kirana Store) -> 409 STORE_CLOSED
# @name agarwal
GET {{base}}/stores/search?q=agarwal
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}

@agarwalId = {{agarwal.response.body.$[0].id}}

### 3.6 (send after 3.5)
POST {{base}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "DIRECT",
  "storeId": {{agarwalId}},
  "lat": 28.5050,
  "lng": 77.3800,
  "items": [ { "name": "Atta", "quantity": 1, "unit": "KG" } ]
}

### 3.7 NEAREST far from every store -> 422 NO_STORES_NEARBY
POST {{base}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "NEAREST",
  "lat": 28.7041,
  "lng": 77.1025,
  "items": [ { "name": "Atta", "quantity": 1, "unit": "KG" } ]
}

### 3.8 Validation -> 400, fields["items[0].quantity"], fields["items[1].unit"]
POST {{base}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "NEAREST",
  "lat": 28.5050,
  "lng": 77.3800,
  "items": [
    { "name": "Atta", "quantity": 0, "unit": "KG" },
    { "name": "Rice", "quantity": 1, "unit": "BORI" }
  ]
}

### 3.9 My requests -> newest first, itemCount, storesSentCount, quotesCount 0, preview (3 names)
GET {{base}}/requests/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}

### 3.10 One request -> items + targets (storeName, area, distanceKm, seen), no phones
GET {{base}}/requests/{{nearestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}

### 3.11 Cancel the DIRECT request -> 200, status CANCELLED
POST {{base}}/requests/{{directId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}

### 3.12 Cancel it again -> 409 INVALID_STATUS
POST {{base}}/requests/{{directId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}

### 3.13 Another customer (Priya) can't see Anita's request -> 404 REQUEST_NOT_FOUND
# @name p3Other
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000003",
  "password": "test123"
}

### 3.14 (send after 3.13)
GET {{base}}/requests/{{nearestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p3Other.response.body.token}}

### ---------------- store side ----------------

### 3.15 Login as Gupta Kirana owner (9000000012) — received the seed requests,
###      3.2 (nearest) and 3.4 (direct)
# @name p3Owner
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000012",
  "password": "test123"
}

@p3o = {{p3Owner.response.body.token}}

### 3.16 Inbox, open only -> newest first, isNew true, distanceKm, preview
GET {{base}}/store/requests?status=OPEN
Authorization: Bearer {{p3o}}

### 3.17 Inbox, closed -> the cancelled DIRECT request from 3.11
GET {{base}}/store/requests?status=CLOSED
Authorization: Bearer {{p3o}}

### 3.18 Open the NEAREST request -> items + distanceKm + seenAt; no customer name/phone/location
GET {{base}}/store/requests/{{nearestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p3o}}

### 3.19 Inbox again -> that request now has isNew false
GET {{base}}/store/requests?status=OPEN
Authorization: Bearer {{p3o}}

### 3.20 Customer view now shows Gupta Kirana as seen: true
GET {{base}}/requests/{{nearestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p3c}}

### 3.21 A store that did NOT receive it (Laxmi Super Mart, 4.6 km) -> 404
# @name p3Far
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000024",
  "password": "test123"
}

### 3.22 (send after 3.21)
GET {{base}}/store/requests/{{nearestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p3Far.response.body.token}}


######################################################################
### PHASE 4 — Quotes. Start the app first (seed quotes are added on
### startup if no quotes exist: seed request #1 gets 3 quotes, #2 gets 2).
### Run 4.1 -> 4.20 top to bottom; ids are captured automatically.
### linePrice = total for the line in rupees, not per unit.
######################################################################

### 4.1 Login as seed customer Anita (9000000001)
# @name p4Customer
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000001",
  "password": "test123"
}

@p4c = {{p4Customer.response.body.token}}

### 4.2 Create a fresh NEAREST request with 3 items -> 201 (Sharma and Gupta are the 2 nearest)
# @name p4Req
POST {{base}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{p4c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "NEAREST",
  "lat": 28.5050,
  "lng": 77.3800,
  "items": [
    { "name": "Aashirvaad atta", "quantity": 5, "unit": "KG" },
    { "name": "Amul butter", "quantity": 500, "unit": "G" },
    { "name": "अंडे", "quantity": 1, "unit": "DOZEN" }
  ]
}

@p4Id = {{p4Req.response.body.id}}
@item1 = {{p4Req.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
@item2 = {{p4Req.response.body.$.items[1].id}}
@item3 = {{p4Req.response.body.$.items[2].id}}

### ---------------- store side: Sharma General Store ----------------

### 4.3 Login as Sharma General Store owner (9000000011, 0.2 km)
# @name p4Sharma
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000011",
  "password": "test123"
}

@p4s = {{p4Sharma.response.body.token}}

### 4.4 Open the request -> items, myQuote: null
GET {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}

### 4.5 Send a quote -> 200, status SUBMITTED, totalPrice 340.00
###     (280 + 60; eggs UNAVAILABLE so their 12/99 is forced to 0; the "totalPrice": 1 is ignored;
###      butter asked 500 G, offered 1 PACKET)
# @name p4Quote
PUT {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "packingTimeMins": 15,
  "totalPrice": 1,
  "items": [
    { "requestItemId": {{item1}}, "offeredQty": 5, "unit": "KG", "linePrice": 280, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item2}}, "offeredQty": 1, "unit": "PACKET", "linePrice": 60, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item3}}, "offeredQty": 12, "unit": "PCS", "linePrice": 99, "status": "UNAVAILABLE" }
  ]
}

### 4.6 Missing an item -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR, fields.items "missing requestItemId ..."
PUT {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "packingTimeMins": 15,
  "items": [
    { "requestItemId": {{item1}}, "offeredQty": 5, "unit": "KG", "linePrice": 280, "status": "AVAILABLE" }
  ]
}

### 4.7 Bad lines -> 400: fields["items[0].linePrice"] must be greater than 0,
###     fields["items[1].offeredQty"] is required, packingTimeMins must be between 5 and 240
PUT {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "packingTimeMins": 300,
  "items": [
    { "requestItemId": {{item1}}, "offeredQty": 5, "unit": "KG", "linePrice": 0, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item2}}, "unit": "PACKET", "linePrice": 60, "status": "PARTIAL" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item3}}, "status": "UNAVAILABLE" }
  ]
}

### 4.8 Update the quote (eggs now PARTIAL: 6 PCS for 42, packing 20) -> 200,
###     SAME quoteId as 4.5, totalPrice 382.00, newer updatedAt
PUT {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "packingTimeMins": 20,
  "items": [
    { "requestItemId": {{item1}}, "offeredQty": 5, "unit": "KG", "linePrice": 280, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item2}}, "offeredQty": 1, "unit": "PACKET", "linePrice": 60, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item3}}, "offeredQty": 6, "unit": "PCS", "linePrice": 42, "status": "PARTIAL" }
  ]
}

### 4.9 Inbox -> this request has myQuoteTotal 382.00 (requests not quoted yet: null)
GET {{base}}/store/requests?status=OPEN
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}

### 4.10 Open it again -> myQuote with the 3 lines, packingTimeMins 20
GET {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}

### ---------------- store side: Gupta Kirana ----------------

### 4.11 Login as Gupta Kirana owner (9000000012, 0.5 km)
# @name p4Gupta
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000012",
  "password": "test123"
}

### 4.12 Gupta quotes everything -> 200, totalPrice 409.00, packing 30
PUT {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{p4Gupta.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "packingTimeMins": 30,
  "items": [
    { "requestItemId": {{item1}}, "offeredQty": 5, "unit": "KG", "linePrice": 275, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item2}}, "offeredQty": 500, "unit": "G", "linePrice": 50, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item3}}, "offeredQty": 1, "unit": "DOZEN", "linePrice": 84, "status": "AVAILABLE" }
  ]
}

### 4.13 A store that did NOT receive it (Laxmi Super Mart, 4.6 km): login
# @name p4Far
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000024",
  "password": "test123"
}

### 4.14 (send after 4.13) Laxmi tries to quote -> 404 REQUEST_NOT_FOUND
PUT {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{p4Far.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "packingTimeMins": 10,
  "items": [
    { "requestItemId": {{item1}}, "offeredQty": 5, "unit": "KG", "linePrice": 1, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item2}}, "offeredQty": 1, "unit": "PACKET", "linePrice": 1, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item3}}, "offeredQty": 1, "unit": "DOZEN", "linePrice": 1, "status": "AVAILABLE" }
  ]
}

### ---------------- customer side ----------------

### 4.15 Customer reads the request -> quotes: Sharma 382.00 (2 available, 1 partial) first,
###      then Gupta 409.00 (3 available); each line shows askedQty/askedUnit vs offeredQty/unit;
###      targets: Sharma and Gupta quoted true, the other 3 false; no store phones
GET {{base}}/requests/{{p4Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p4c}}

### 4.16 My requests -> this one: quotesCount 2, lowestTotal 382.00
GET {{base}}/requests/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{p4c}}

### 4.17 Seed request #1 (Anita's) -> 3 seed quotes, one with an UNAVAILABLE line (Doodh)
GET {{base}}/requests/1
Authorization: Bearer {{p4c}}

### ---------------- cancel rejects quotes ----------------

### 4.18 Cancel the request -> 200 CANCELLED, both quotes status REJECTED
POST {{base}}/requests/{{p4Id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{p4c}}

### 4.19 Sharma tries to update the quote -> 409 REQUEST_CLOSED
PUT {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "packingTimeMins": 20,
  "items": [
    { "requestItemId": {{item1}}, "offeredQty": 5, "unit": "KG", "linePrice": 270, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item2}}, "offeredQty": 1, "unit": "PACKET", "linePrice": 60, "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    { "requestItemId": {{item3}}, "offeredQty": 6, "unit": "PCS", "linePrice": 42, "status": "PARTIAL" }
  ]
}

### 4.20 Sharma's view -> request CANCELLED, myQuote.status REJECTED
GET {{base}}/store/requests/{{p4Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p4s}}


######################################################################
### PHASE 5 — Accept and lock, contacts, Ready, Picked up, history.
### Self-contained and re-runnable: makes a fresh request each time.
### Run 5.1 -> 5.24 top to bottom; ids and the pickup code are captured.
######################################################################

### 5.1 Login as seed customer Anita (9000000001)
# @name p5Customer
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000001",
  "password": "test123"
}

@p5c = {{p5Customer.response.body.token}}

### 5.2 Create a NEAREST request -> 201 (goes to Sharma 0.2 km, Gupta 0.5 km, ...)
# @name p5Req
POST {{base}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{p5c}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "NEAREST",
  "lat": 28.5050,
  "lng": 77.3800,
  "items": [
    { "name": "Aashirvaad atta", "quantity": 5, "unit": "KG" },
    { "name": "Tata salt", "quantity": 1, "unit": "KG" }
  ]
}

@p5Id = {{p5Req.response.body.id}}
@p5i1 = {{p5Req.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
@p5i2 = {{p5Req.response.body.$.items[1].id}}

### 5.3 Login as Sharma General Store owner (9000000011)
# @name p5Sharma
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "9000000011",
  "password": "test123"
}

